"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The  NFCSmartCardConnection is short lived and should be closed as soon as the commands sent to the YubiKey have finished processing. It is up to the user of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the connection to close it when it no longer is needed. As long as the connection is open the NFC modal will cover the lower part of the iPhone screen.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In addition to the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/NFCSmartCardConnection\/close(error:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" method defined in the SmartCardConnection protocol the NFCSmartCardConnection has an additional ","type":"text"},{"code":"close(success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"method that will close the connection and set the alertMessage of the NFC alert to the provided message.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"NFC is only supported on iPhones from iPhone 6 and forward. It will not work on iPads since there’s no NFC chip in these devices."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"NFC connection to a YubiKey (iOS only)."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"NFCSmartCardConnection establishes a connection to a YubiKey via NFC. The connection","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"presents the system NFC dialog and waits for the user to tap their YubiKey.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"NFC connections are short-lived due to iOS timeout constraints. Perform operations quickly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and close the connection with a user-visible message."}]},{"code":["let connection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection(","    alertMessag